			"notes": "# Nova Raids v1.0.0 - Out of Beta!\n\nNova Raids is finally out of Beta! This update is effectively a full internal rewrite: persistent raid queues and history that survive server restarts, a brand-new Category Modifiers system for randomized boss variants, an all-new per-phase Events system (sounds/titles/particles/commands/Discord webhooks), a full item/reward overhaul with native item component support, and a complete placeholder system rewrite.\n\n**This is a big one. Please read the Breaking Changes section before updating your server.**\n\n## ⚠️ Breaking Changes\n- **All placeholders changed format.** The old dot-notation placeholders (`%boss.species%`, `%raid.player.place%`, `%boss.form%`, etc.) no longer work anywhere, with no fallback — they'll render literally instead of resolving. See the new placeholders list in the wiki for the new flat format (`%boss_species%`, or `%novaraids:boss_species%` with PlaceholderAPI).\n- **Item-based config fields (vouchers, passes, raid balls, item rewards) now use full item objects** (`{\"id\": \"minecraft:...\", \"count\": 1}`) instead of a bare item ID plus a separate `*_data` field. The `*_data` fields are gone — put item component data inside the item object itself.\n- **`config.json`'s `default_voucher`, `default_pass`, and `passes_enabled` options are removed.** Vouchers and passes no longer fall back to a shared default template.\n- **Pokémon reward presets use a completely new schema** — Cobblemon's native `PokemonProperties` format (`SpeciesText`, `Level`, `Shiny`, etc.) instead of NovaRaids' old custom species/level/ability/nature/form/features/gender/shiny/scale/held_item/moves/ivs/evs fields.\n- **Reward pools and presets changed structure**: `rolls: {min, max}` is now flat `min_rolls`/`max_rolls`, and every reward entry now needs a `\"type\": \"unset\"` (inline) or `\"type\": \"preset\"` (by-id) discriminator.\n- **`NovaRaids/bosses/` is renamed to `NovaRaids/categories/`.** This is auto-migrated on load, so your server will rename the folder for you — but any external tooling/scripts pointing at the old path will break.\n- **`locations.json` boss position fields are renested** under a new `boss_location` object, and `boss_facing_direction` is replaced by `yaw`/`pitch` inside it.\n- **`schedules.json` field renames**: `bounds: {min, max}` → `min_seconds`/`max_seconds`; a category schedule's `category` key → `category_id`.\n- **Discord webhook config moved** from `messages.json > discord` to `config.json > discord_webhook`, with several fields renamed (`webhook_toggle`→`enabled`, `webhook_url`→`url`, `webhook_username`→`username`, `webhook_avatar_url`→`avatar_url`). The old fixed `raid_start`/`raid_running`/`raid_end`/`raid_failed` embed sections are gone — Discord content is now defined per raid-phase in the new Events system, and `role_ping` is gone (put your role mention directly in an event's message text instead).\n- **`messages.json` is restructured.** The old flat `messages.*` phase-announcement block (`start_pre_phase`, `boss_defeated`, `catch_phase_end`, etc.) is gone — that text now lives in the Events system. Everything else moved under `commands.*`, `feedback.*` (with a nested `warnings.*`), and `leaderboard.*`, with several keys renamed (e.g. `give_command_*` → `commands.give*`, `warning_*` → `feedback.warnings.*`).\n- **`config.json`'s `automatic_battle_delay_seconds` is renamed to `automatic_battle_delay`.**\n\nA config migration guide (and converter tool) will be linked from the wiki — if you're updating an existing server, back up your `NovaRaids/` config folder first.\n\n## Major New Features\n\n..."
		},
